{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "When working with active_record, you often need to establish if a row exists to see if you can do operations against it.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/09ba04f71eb628ee50af5c32b18d8d078a4d42292504e0a01c74e15d3c3d4439.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.66], [4, 2.12, 2.3], [5, 2.3, 2.64], [6, 2.64, 2.86], [7, 2.86, 3.02], [8, 3.02, 3.44], [11, 3.64, 3.88], [12, 3.88, 4.28], [13, 4.28, 4.72], [14, 4.72, 4.92], [15, 4.92, 5.04], [16, 5.04, 5.14], [17, 5.14, 5.3], [18, 5.3, 5.44], [19, 5.44, 6.0], [20, 6.0, 6.36], [21, 6.36, 6.7]]}, {"text": "Here is an interesting technique when checking if objects or relations exist in a collection.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c3d663cdab2945e2fa24e3955011b88e80f75e084c465e02e3ddd020aa10a6b7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.76], [10, 2.76, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 3.86], [13, 3.86, 3.94], [14, 3.94, 4.3]]}, {"text": "Many developers use the present?", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a2b1c834f083d7a589f88a136617847153087f07cd485d9429b74c407d265735.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.84], [2, 0.84, 1.22], [3, 1.22, 1.34], [4, 1.34, 1.66]]}, {"text": "method, but this is bad practice, because it performs a standard SELECT query against your table which, relative to a count, is very slow.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1c074c1e15e578f4fb28738aaae22e229b9b66a76f43ad49a94bb3ee1965ac00.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.54, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.24], [8, 2.24, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.1], [11, 3.1, 3.5], [12, 3.5, 3.88], [13, 3.88, 4.32], [14, 4.32, 4.6], [15, 4.6, 4.86], [16, 4.86, 5.18], [17, 5.18, 5.6], [18, 5.6, 5.9], [21, 6.26, 6.84], [22, 6.84, 7.12], [23, 7.12, 7.46]]}, {"text": "The better trick would be to use the exits?", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5fb70dad2f3f869ddd1b611c70515e553b02ac43be57fc656374086dcb8a7735.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.04], [6, 1.04, 1.3], [7, 1.3, 1.48]]}, {"text": "method to more efficiently determine if a record exists since it just has to return a number instead of a large collection of objects", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1ae623af49ee967f9d9098bceb3b852e01ce6410843963e302563f405b1fbcbc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.38, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.22], [4, 1.22, 1.78], [5, 1.78, 2.0], [6, 2.0, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.32], [8, 2.32, 2.82], [9, 2.82, 3.18], [10, 3.18, 3.36], [11, 3.36, 3.54], [12, 3.54, 3.76], [13, 3.76, 3.9], [14, 3.9, 4.2], [15, 4.2, 4.38], [16, 4.38, 4.68], [17, 4.68, 5.0], [18, 5.0, 5.14], [19, 5.14, 5.2], [20, 5.2, 5.46], [21, 5.46, 5.88], [22, 5.88, 6.04], [23, 6.04, 6.38]]}, {"text": "Alternatively, if you know you are going to need the object later, it is better to just load exactly what you need and use it later:", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ee78ba369afd3da05e87f1649d4178e34eef9104f395268b67932e2a1ef8a54d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.66], [1, 1.3, 1.48], [2, 1.48, 1.58], [3, 1.58, 1.76], [4, 1.76, 1.94], [5, 1.94, 2.02], [6, 2.02, 2.2], [7, 2.2, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.52], [9, 2.52, 2.66], [10, 2.66, 2.94], [11, 2.94, 3.34], [12, 3.8, 3.96], [13, 3.96, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.28], [15, 4.28, 4.48], [16, 4.48, 4.66], [17, 4.66, 4.9], [18, 4.9, 5.36], [19, 5.36, 5.74], [20, 5.74, 5.88], [21, 5.88, 6.1], [22, 6.1, 6.36], [23, 6.36, 6.56], [24, 6.56, 6.7], [25, 6.7, 6.98]]}, {"text": "If you had done a exists or a count on the post, then you would have to run back to the database to fetch the rest of the objects.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/764830edb44fc830a1d77e262b484f2b25eb91821e4f229b06c2aa8996b659a3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.78], [5, 0.78, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.74], [9, 2.1, 2.42], [10, 2.42, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.92], [12, 3.32, 3.42], [13, 3.42, 3.5], [14, 3.5, 3.62], [15, 3.62, 3.76], [16, 3.76, 3.96], [17, 3.96, 4.22], [18, 4.22, 4.54], [19, 4.54, 4.74], [20, 4.74, 4.84], [21, 4.84, 5.2], [22, 5.2, 5.58], [23, 5.58, 5.86], [24, 5.86, 6.06], [25, 6.06, 6.26], [26, 6.26, 6.44], [27, 6.44, 6.56], [28, 6.56, 6.9]]}, {"text": "While this is more memory intensive, it can be much faster technique.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2a7114c6ee5a6f67d99dbdfa70ccf8a9112d699be99162502ed8c5ac4ce4cb51.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.64], [4, 0.64, 0.92], [5, 0.92, 1.4], [6, 1.7, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 1.86], [8, 1.86, 1.96], [9, 1.96, 2.14], [10, 2.14, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.92]]}]}